{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://docs.oasis-open.org/sarif/sarif/v2.1.0/errata01/os/schemas/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "grype",
          "version": "0.116.1",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-13221-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-13221 critical vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Perl versions through 5.43.9 produce silently incorrect regular expression matches when an alternation of more than 65535 fixed string branches is compiled into a trie in Perl_study_chunk.  When such branches are combined into a trie, the delta between the first branch and the shared tail is stored in a 16-bit field. A branch count above 65535 overflows the field, and the trie's match decision table is truncated with no warning or error.  A pattern of this shape produces false positive matches (matching strings it should not) and false negative matches (failing to match strings it should). When such a pattern gates an access or filtering decision, the result is wrong."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-13221",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-13221\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.42.2-3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-13221](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-13221)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-13221**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | perl-base  | 5.42.2-3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-13221](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-13221)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/perl-base@5.42.2-3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-42496-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-42496 critical vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Archive::Tar versions before 3.08 for Perl extract symlinks with attacker controlled targets outside the extraction directory.  _make_special_file() passes the tar header's linkname to symlink() without validating it against absolute paths or .. segments. The secure-extract mode check that guards regular file extraction does not cover the symlink target.  A subsequent open through the extracted name reads or writes the attacker chosen path."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-42496",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-42496\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.42.2-3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-42496](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-42496)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-42496**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | perl-base  | 5.42.2-3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-42496](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-42496)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/perl-base@5.42.2-3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2017-17740-libldap2",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2017-17740 low vulnerability for libldap2 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "contrib/slapd-modules/nops/nops.c in OpenLDAP through 2.4.45, when both the nops module and the memberof overlay are enabled, attempts to free a buffer that was allocated on the stack, which allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (slapd crash) via a member MODDN operation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2017-17740",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2017-17740\nSeverity: low\nPackage: libldap2\nVersion: 2.6.13+dfsg-1+b1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2017-17740](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2017-17740)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2017-17740**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | libldap2  | 2.6.13+dfsg-1+b1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2017-17740](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2017-17740)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libldap2@2.6.13%2Bdfsg-1%2Bb1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=openldap%402.6.13%2Bdfsg-1"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-12087-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-12087 critical vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Socket versions before 2.041 for Perl have an out-of-bounds heap read.  In Socket.xs, pack_ip_mreq_source() checks the length of its source argument before the argument is read, so the check tests the byte length carried over from the preceding multiaddr argument instead. Both addresses occupy a 4-byte field, so a valid multiaddr lets a source of any length pass the check, and the source is then copied into the 4-byte imr_sourceaddr field with a fixed-size copy. A source shorter than 4 bytes is not rejected, and the copy reads up to 3 bytes past the end of its buffer.  Calling pack_ip_mreq_source() with a source value shorter than 4 bytes copies adjacent heap memory into the returned packed structure."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-12087",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-12087\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.42.2-3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-12087](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-12087)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-12087**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | perl-base  | 5.42.2-3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-12087](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-12087)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/perl-base@5.42.2-3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-9538-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-9538 high vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Archive::Tar versions before 3.10 for Perl allow memory exhaustion via attacker controlled entry size field in tar header.  _read_tar() reads each entry's payload with $handle-\u003eread($$data, $block), where $block is derived from the entry's 12-byte size field in the tar header with no upper bound on that value.  A crafted header declaring a multi-gigabyte size causes Perl to allocate a scalar of that size."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-9538",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-9538\nSeverity: high\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.42.2-3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-9538](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-9538)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-9538**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | perl-base  | 5.42.2-3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-9538](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-9538)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/perl-base@5.42.2-3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-42497-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-42497 high vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Archive::Tar versions before 3.08 for Perl extract hardlinks to attacker controlled paths outside the extraction directory.  _make_special_file() passes the tar header's linkname to link() without validating it against absolute paths or .. segments, creating a hardlink that shares the victim file's inode.  A subsequent write through the extracted name modifies the victim file, and the post-extraction chmod, chown, and utime block in _extract_file() (guarded only against symlinks via -l) applies the tar header's mode, owner, and timestamps to the shared inode during extraction alone."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-42497",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-42497\nSeverity: high\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.42.2-3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-42497](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-42497)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-42497**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | perl-base  | 5.42.2-3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-42497](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-42497)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/perl-base@5.42.2-3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2018-20796-libc-bin",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2018-20796 low vulnerability for libc-bin package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the GNU C Library (aka glibc or libc6) through 2.29, check_dst_limits_calc_pos_1 in posix/regexec.c has Uncontrolled Recursion, as demonstrated by '(\\227|)(\\\\1\\\\1|t1|\\\\\\2537)+' in grep."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2018-20796",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2018-20796\nSeverity: low\nPackage: libc-bin\nVersion: 2.42-17\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2018-20796](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2018-20796)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2018-20796**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | libc-bin  | 2.42-17  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2018-20796](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2018-20796)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
