            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41992-gzip",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-41992 high vulnerability for gzip package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "GNU gzip contains a global buffer overflow vulnerability in the LZH decompression logic caused by improper reuse of shared global state between different decompression formats within a single execution. GNU gzip maintains a global array that is shared across the LZ77, LZW, and LZH decompression routines and is not reinitialized between files processed in the same invocation. By decompressing a specially crafted LZW file followed by a specially crafted LZH file in a single gzip -d command, an attacker can poison the shared global state and subsequently trigger an out‑of‑bounds read in the LZH decoder. The LZH decompression logic follows stale values left in the shared array, causing reads past the end of the allocated global buffer.  This issue has been fixed in the commit 63dbf6b3b9e6e781df1a6a64e609b10e23969681"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-41992",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-41992\nSeverity: high\nPackage: gzip\nVersion: 1.13-1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-41992](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-41992)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-41992**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | gzip  | 1.13-1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-41992](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-41992)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/gzip@1.13-1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-6238-libc-bin",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-6238 medium vulnerability for libc-bin package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The deprecated functions ns_printrrf, ns_printrr and fp_nquery in the GNU C Library version 2.0.1 to version 2.43 fail to validate the RDATA content against the RDATA length in a DNS response when processing A6, CERT, LOC, TKEY or TSIG records, which may allow an attacker to craft a DNS response, causing a target application to crash or read uninitialized memory.  These functions are for application debugging only and hence not in the path of code executed by the DNS resolver.  Further, they have been deprecated since version 2.34 and should not be used by any new applications.  Applications should consider porting away from these interfaces since they may be removed in future versions."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-6238",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-6238\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libc-bin\nVersion: 2.42-17\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-6238](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-6238)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-6238**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libc-bin  | 2.42-17  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-6238](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-6238)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libc-bin@2.42-17?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=glibc"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.5"
              }
            },
